      <h2>What Is OLED Burn-In?</h2>
      <p>
        Burn-in is permanent or semi-permanent discoloration left on a display when its pixels age unevenly. On an OLED or AMOLED panel
        every pixel generates its own light and dims a little each hour it is lit, so brightness is spent per pixel rather than drawn from
