      <h2>What Is a Dead Pixel?</h2>
      <p>
        A dead pixel is a single point on your display that no longer lights up at all. It receives no power, so it stays black no matter
        what the screen is showing — it does not flicker, change color, or respond to anything you do. Against a bright background it
        reads as a tiny dark speck that never moves, which is why a full white or light-colored screen is the fastest way to find one.
